{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>שונאך</b> Two times in the Masorah: חמור שונאך. אם רעב שונאך האכילהו לחם. Because here it treats two kinds of enemies: an idolater and an Israelite. Regarding the idolater enemy, from the seven nations we derive: וחדלת מעזוב לו. Regarding the Israelite enemy: עזוב תעזוב עמו." "<b>רובץ</b> Three times in the Masorah. And the others: לפתח חטאת רובץ. רובץ בין המשפתים. לפתח חטאת רובץ — this is the evil inclination, that if one followed his inclination and multiplied sin until he is רובץ beneath its burden — what is his remedy? Let him engage in Torah, like Issachar, who was רובץ between the sheepfolds, as we say: if this wretch encounters you — drag him to the study hall." "<b>(י י\"א) את תבואתה</b> And the seventh year. To forbid the produce of the eve of the seventh year that entered the seventh year."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:12.097383429Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}